WEBVTT

00:00:00.181 --> 00:00:03.620
Secure cameras before connecting them to a monitoring system.

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:07.315
Change default credentials, use unique accounts, disable unused services,

00:00:07.315 --> 00:00:10.465
apply supported updates, and avoid direct internet exposure.

00:00:10.465 --> 00:00:14.240
Inventory model, firmware, owner, network address, and update status.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:16.900
Segment cameras, NVRs, inference servers, storage,

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:20.144
and administrative systems according to required communication.

00:00:20.144 --> 00:00:23.740
Firewalls should permit only necessary streams and management paths.

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:27.640
Remote access should use a controlled entry point with strong authentication and logging.

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:30.560
Protect stored video, thumbnails, metadata, model prompts,

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:34.980
and review notes with encryption where appropriate, access control, and retention policy.

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:39.105
Local AI servers require operating-system and driver patching, least privilege,

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:42.930
secure administration, and protection of API keys or alert credentials.

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:46.110
Back up configuration, camera maps, rules, model versions,

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:48.885
and review metadata according to recovery needs.

00:00:48.885 --> 00:00:51.955
Test restoration without retaining more video than policy permits.

00:00:51.955 --> 00:00:55.185
Keep a known-good way to rebuild or replace the inference host.

00:00:55.185 --> 00:00:59.075
Monitor the complete pipeline: camera reachability, stream decode, frame rate,

00:00:59.075 --> 00:01:03.780
inference latency, accelerator health, storage capacity, event creation, dashboard access,

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:04.880
and alert delivery.

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:09.465
A green server status is not enough if the camera is frozen or notifications are failing.

00:01:09.465 --> 00:01:10.920
Define fail-safe expectations.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:13.090
When the model, network, or camera is unavailable,

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:17.015
the system should report degraded coverage rather than imply normal awareness.

00:01:17.015 --> 00:01:19.290
Practice incident response, preserve relevant logs,

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:23.370
and restore trustworthy operation without broadening data access during the emergency.
